abstract: >
  Applied Ontology Methods™ is the only body of work that operates at the
  intersection of Applied, Ontological, and Method to produce measurable,
  observable, and permanent transformation in human performance. Developed
  by Paul Roth over more than two decades, it comprises six complete Methods —
  each with its own Tool, Training, and Technology of Transformation — and
  is delivered through an AI-driven pre-print modular learning architecture
  designed to scale to millions independent of any practitioner.
